  "title": "Saudi-led coalition strengthens maritime defenses in Yemen",
  "summary": "Saudi Arabia has established a maritime defense coalition to protect vital waterways in the Red Sea, while also coordinating with other countries to counter Houthi attacks on shipping and energy routes.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Saudi Arabia has formed a maritime defense coalition with over a dozen countries to protect its Red Sea shipping routes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The coalition includes countries like Egypt, Turkey, and Sudan, which have pledged to support Saudi efforts.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The coalition aims to deter Houthi attacks on vital maritime infrastructure.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
